  "notepad": {
    "activeNoteIndex": 0,
    "notes": [
      {
        "name": "How to read this sheet",
        "content": "WHAT THIS SHEET IS\n\n7 carrier controls, one per language, each holding a handler for all\n55 events the panel API defines — 385 scripts in one document.\n\nHOW TO RUN THE PASS\n\n  1. Open the Scripts tab. Every carrier should list its full set with no blanks.\n  2. Click into a handful per language. The body should name the right function for the\n     event and be written in that language — not a Lua body under a Python badge.\n  3. Run Validate. A language whose toolchain is absent reports SKIP, which is not a\n     failure; a language whose toolchain is present and reports errors is.\n  4. Check the tiles: each caption is the handler name and its group, each body the payload\n     the handler receives. A tile reading \"—\" takes no payload.\n\nWHAT A FAILURE LOOKS LIKE\n\n  - an empty script body for a language/event pair\n  - a handler named for a different event than its caption\n  - the same body under two different languages\n  - an event in the API that has no row here (the generator is stale — re-run it)\n\nWHAT IT CANNOT PROVE\n\nThat the events FIRE. This is an authoring-path sheet: it proves the editor can make every\nhandler, not that the runtime calls them. Firing is covered by scriptFlow, scriptTimersState\nand scriptMidiInHandles in the test suite, and by QA-05 for the verbs a handler would call."
      }
    ]
  },
  "viewer": {
    "images": [],
    "activeImageIndex": 0
  },
  "requiredProfiles": [],
  "parameterSnapshots": {},
  "exportParameters": [],
  "scripts": [],
  "scripting": {
    "enabled": true,
    "runInPreview": true,
    "runOnExport": true
  },
  "controls": [
    {
      "_children": {
        "Core": {"name":"group_lua_55_handlers_one_per_event","id":"qa_group_0","controlType":"Label"},
        "Transform": {"x":28,"y":28,"width":1544,"height":26},
        "Background": {"_children":{"Fill":{"colour":"FF23282D"},"Border":{"thickness":1,"colour":"3389C2FF"},"Corners":{"radius":4}}},
        "Text": {"content":"lua — 55 handlers, one per event","_children":{"Font":{"size":13,"bold":true}}},
        "ContentLayout": {"horizontalAlign":"left","paddingLeft":10,"paddingRight":10,"paddingTop":3,"paddingBottom":3}
      },
      "_type": "Control"
    },
    {
      "_children": {
        "Core": {"name":"caption_qa_cap_0","id":"qa_cap_0","controlType":"Label"},
        "Transform": {"x":28,"y":64,"width":210,"height":18},
        "Background": {"_children":{"Fill":{"colour":"00000000"}}},
        "Text": {"content":"lua carrier","_children":{"Font":{"size":11}}},
        "ContentLayout": {"horizontalAlign":"left","paddingLeft":2,"paddingRight":2,"paddingTop":0,"paddingBottom":0}
      },
      "_type": "Control"
    },
    {
      "_children": {
        "Core": {"name":"scripts_lua","id":"qa04_carrier_lua","controlType":"Label"},
        "Transform": {"x":28,"y":86,"width":210,"height":54},
        "Background": {"_children":{"Fill":{"colour":"FF20262B"},"Border":{"thickness":1,"colour":"5589C2FF"},"Corners":{"radius":4}}},
        "Text": {"content":"lua\n55 handlers"},
        "Scripts": {"_type":"Scripts","_children":{"qa04_lua_valueChange":{"id":"qa04_lua_valueChange","name":"lua: onValueChange","language":"lua","source":"function onValueChange(value)\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onValueChange","enabled":true,"description":"Runs again and again while the value moves, as a knob is dragged: for what on screen follows the control.","group":""},"qa04_lua_valueChanged":{"id":"qa04_lua_valueChanged","name":"lua: onValueChanged","language":"lua","source":"function onValueChanged(value)\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onValueChanged","enabled":true,"description":"Runs once, when the value settles, as a knob is let go: the moment to tell the synth.","group":""},"qa04_lua_activeHandleChanged":{"id":"qa04_lua_activeHandleChanged","name":"lua: onActiveHandleChanged","language":"lua","source":"function onActiveHandleChanged(info)\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onActiveHandleChanged","enabled":true,"description":"A slider with more than one handle moved to another handle. `info.activeHandle` and `info.previousActiveHandle` are each \"start\", \"current\" or \"end\".","group":""},"qa04_lua_click":{"id":"qa04_lua_click","name":"lua: onClick","language":"lua","source":"function onClick(mouse)\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onClick","enabled":true,"description":"The control was clicked. `mouse.x` and `mouse.y` say where, inside the control.","group":""},"qa04_lua_doubleClick":{"id":"qa04_lua_doubleClick","name":"lua: onDoubleClick","language":"lua","source":"function onDoubleClick(mouse)\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onDoubleClick","enabled":true,"description":"The control was double-clicked. `mouse.x` and `mouse.y` say where.","group":""},"qa04_lua_pointerDown":{"id":"qa04_lua_pointerDown","name":"lua: onPointerDown","language":"lua","source":"function onPointerDown(mouse)\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onPointerDown","enabled":true,"description":"A mouse button was pressed on the control. `mouse.x` and `mouse.y` say where, `mouse.button` which button, and `mouse.modifiers` the keys held.","group":""},"qa04_lua_pointerMove":{"id":"qa04_lua_pointerMove","name":"lua: onPointerMove","language":"lua","source":"function onPointerMove(mouse)\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onPointerMove","enabled":true,"description":"The mouse moved while a button was held down on the control. `mouse.x` and `mouse.y` give the new position.","group":""},"qa04_lua_pointerUp":{"id":"qa04_lua_pointerUp","name":"lua: onPointerUp","language":"lua","source":"function onPointerUp(mouse)\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onPointerUp","enabled":true,"description":"The mouse button was released.","group":""},"qa04_lua_hoverStart":{"id":"qa04_lua_hoverStart","name":"lua: onHoverStart","language":"lua","source":"function onHoverStart()\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onHoverStart","enabled":true,"description":"The mouse pointer moved onto the control.","group":""},"qa04_lua_hoverEnd":{"id":"qa04_lua_hoverEnd","name":"lua: onHoverEnd","language":"lua","source":"function onHoverEnd()\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onHoverEnd","enabled":true,"description":"The mouse pointer left the control.","group":""},"qa04_lua_wheel":{"id":"qa04_lua_wheel","name":"lua: onWheel","language":"lua","source":"function onWheel(wheel)\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onWheel","enabled":true,"description":"The mouse wheel was turned over the control. `wheel.delta` says how far, and in which direction.","group":""},"qa04_lua_stateChanged":{"id":"qa04_lua_stateChanged","name":"lua: onStateChanged","language":"lua","source":"function onStateChanged(state)\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onStateChanged","enabled":true,"description":"The control's look changed. `state` is \"normal\", \"hover\", \"pressed\" or \"disabled\".","group":""},"qa04_lua_controlChanged":{"id":"qa04_lua_controlChanged","name":"lua: onControlChanged","language":"lua","source":"function onControlChanged(info)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onControlChanged","enabled":true,"description":"A control on the panel changed. `info.target` is its name and `info.value` its new value: one handler for many controls.","group":""},"qa04_lua_timer":{"id":"qa04_lua_timer","name":"lua: onTimer","language":"lua","source":"function onTimer(info)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onTimer","enabled":true,"description":"A timer you started is due. `info.id` is the name you gave it in `ce.time.startTimer()` or `ce.time.syncTimer()`.","group":""},"qa04_lua_keyDown":{"id":"qa04_lua_keyDown","name":"lua: onKeyDown","language":"lua","source":"function onKeyDown(key)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onKeyDown","enabled":true,"description":"A key went down that nothing else on the panel kept: not while typing, and not the panic key, a shortcut, a piano key or a key the focused control used. `key.key` is its name as printed (\"R\", \"7\", \"Space\", \"Up\", \"F2\"), `key.code` its place, the same on every layout (\"KeyR\"), `key.ctrl`, `key.shift`, `key.alt` and `key.meta` the modifiers, `key.repeat` true while the system repeats a held key, and `key.control` the control that has the keyboard. Return true to keep the key: it then goes no further, not to the DAW and not to the editor.","group":""},"qa04_lua_keyUp":{"id":"qa04_lua_keyUp","name":"lua: onKeyUp","language":"lua","source":"function onKeyUp(key)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onKeyUp","enabled":true,"description":"A key whose keyDown was raised went up, with the same fields except `repeat`. Also raised for every such key when the panel loses the keyboard while it is held. Its return value is not used.","group":""},"qa04_lua_beat":{"id":"qa04_lua_beat","name":"lua: onBeat","language":"lua","source":"function onBeat(time)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onBeat","enabled":true,"description":"A beat went by while the transport plays. `time.bar` and `time.beat` give where, `time.beats` the beats so far, and `time.bpm` the tempo. Within a thirtieth of a second: right for a light or a display, not for timing sound.","group":""},"qa04_lua_bar":{"id":"qa04_lua_bar","name":"lua: onBar","language":"lua","source":"function onBar(time)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onBar","enabled":true,"description":"A bar began, on the downbeat, with onBeat. `time.bar` is its number, `time.beats` the beats so far, and `time.beatsPerBar` the beats in a bar.","group":""},"qa04_lua_transport":{"id":"qa04_lua_transport","name":"lua: onTransport","language":"lua","source":"function onTransport(time)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onTransport","enabled":true,"description":"The transport started, stopped or changed tempo. `time.playing` says whether it runs, `time.bpm` gives the tempo and `time.source` what drives it.","group":""},"qa04_lua_parameterReceived":{"id":"qa04_lua_parameterReceived","name":"lua: onParameterReceived","language":"lua","source":"function onParameterReceived(info)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onParameterReceived","enabled":true,"description":"The synth sent a parameter's value, read through its profile. `info.parameter` is the parameter's id and `info.value` its value, in the parameter's own units.","group":""},"qa04_lua_dumpReceived":{"id":"qa04_lua_dumpReceived","name":"lua: onDumpReceived","language":"lua","source":"function onDumpReceived(dump)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onDumpReceived","enabled":true,"description":"A dump from the synth arrived and was read; the controls bound to it are filled in already. `dump.values` holds each value by parameter id, `dump.kind` names the dump, such as \"patch\", and `dump.role` the synth it came from.","group":""},"qa04_lua_oscIn":{"id":"qa04_lua_oscIn","name":"lua: onOscIn","language":"lua","source":"function onOscIn(message)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onOscIn","enabled":true,"description":"An OSC message arrived on the port ce.osc.listen() opened. `message.address` is where it was sent, `message.args` its values, `message.types` their OSC types, `message.from` who sent it ({ host, port }), and `message.time` a bundle's time. origin() gives \"osc\".","group":""},"qa04_lua_automationIn":{"id":"qa04_lua_automationIn","name":"lua: onAutomationIn","language":"lua","source":"function onAutomationIn(move)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onAutomationIn","enabled":true,"description":"The DAW moved a parameter. `move.control` is the control's name, `move.path` its path, `move.value` the new value in the control's own range and `move.id` the DAW parameter's id. The control's own value events fire too, with origin() giving \"host\". Never for a change a script or a hand made.","group":""},"qa04_lua_dawProgramIn":{"id":"qa04_lua_dawProgramIn","name":"lua: onDawProgramIn","language":"lua","source":"function onDawProgramIn(program)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onDawProgramIn","enabled":true,"description":"The DAW chose a program from the plug-in's bank, and the plug-in has sent it to the synth. `program.index` counts from 0, `program.number` from 1, and `program.name` is its name.","group":""},"qa04_lua_ciDiscovered":{"id":"qa04_lua_ciDiscovered","name":"lua: onCiDiscovered","language":"lua","source":"function onCiDiscovered(device)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onCiDiscovered","enabled":true,"description":"A MIDI-CI device answered: to ce.ci.discover(), or by announcing itself. `device` is as ce.ci.discover() describes it: `device.muid`, `device.model`, `device.names` and `device.matchesProfile` among them.","group":""},"qa04_lua_ciDeviceRemoved":{"id":"qa04_lua_ciDeviceRemoved","name":"lua: onCiDeviceRemoved","language":"lua","source":"function onCiDeviceRemoved(device)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onCiDeviceRemoved","enabled":true,"description":"A MIDI-CI device is gone. `device.muid` is its number and `device.role` the panel's device it was found on. Its subscriptions have ended.","group":""},"qa04_lua_ciProfileChanged":{"id":"qa04_lua_ciProfileChanged","name":"lua: onCiProfileChanged","language":"lua","source":"function onCiProfileChanged(profile)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onCiProfileChanged","enabled":true,"description":"A MIDI-CI profile was turned on or off, by a script or on the device itself. `profile.muid` is the device, `profile.id` the profile, `profile.address` \"device\" or a channel, and `profile.enabled` its new state.","group":""},"qa04_lua_verifyDone":{"id":"qa04_lua_verifyDone","name":"lua: onVerifyDone","language":"lua","source":"function onVerifyDone(report)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onVerifyDone","enabled":true,"description":"A ce.verify check finished. `report` is the report its function was given: `report.kind` says which check, `report.ok` whether all was well, and `report.matched`, `report.differed` and `report.unchecked` say what was found. Raised for cancelled checks too.","group":""},"qa04_lua_presetChange":{"id":"qa04_lua_presetChange","name":"lua: onPresetChange","language":"lua","source":"function onPresetChange(preset)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onPresetChange","enabled":true,"description":"The preset changed. `preset.slot`, `preset.program`, `preset.name`, `preset.category` and `preset.bankId` describe it; `preset.source` is \"device\" when the synth sent a Program Change, \"panel\" when the panel called recallPreset.","group":""},"qa04_lua_midiIn":{"id":"qa04_lua_midiIn","name":"lua: onMidiIn","language":"lua","source":"function onMidiIn(midi)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onMidiIn","enabled":true,"description":"A MIDI message arrived. `midi.bytes` holds it as received, `midi.status` its first byte and `midi.channel` its channel, counted from 0. `midi.from` is the device it came from.","group":""},"qa04_lua_ccIn":{"id":"qa04_lua_ccIn","name":"lua: onCcIn","language":"lua","source":"function onCcIn(cc)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onCcIn","enabled":true,"description":"A controller message arrived. `cc.cc` is the controller number and `cc.value` its value; `cc.channel` counts from 0 here, 0 to 15, where sendCC and onNoteIn count 1 to 16. `cc.from` is the device it came from.","group":""},"qa04_lua_noteIn":{"id":"qa04_lua_noteIn","name":"lua: onNoteIn","language":"lua","source":"function onNoteIn(note)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onNoteIn","enabled":true,"description":"A note was played. `note.channel`, 1 to 16 as in sendNote, `note.note` and `note.velocity` describe it. A note-on at velocity 0 is a note-off in MIDI, and arrives as onNoteOffIn. `note.from` is the device it came from, and `note.id` the note's id while ce.mpe.listen() reads that device.","group":""},"qa04_lua_noteOffIn":{"id":"qa04_lua_noteOffIn","name":"lua: onNoteOffIn","language":"lua","source":"function onNoteOffIn(note)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onNoteOffIn","enabled":true,"description":"A note was let go. `note.channel`, 1 to 16, `note.note` and `note.velocity` describe it; the velocity is the release velocity, or 0 for a note-on at velocity 0. `note.from` and `note.id` are as onNoteIn gives them.","group":""},"qa04_lua_bendIn":{"id":"qa04_lua_bendIn","name":"lua: onBendIn","language":"lua","source":"function onBendIn(bend)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onBendIn","enabled":true,"description":"A pitch bend arrived. `bend.value` is -8192 to 8191, 0 in the middle; `bend.amount` the same from -1 to 1; `bend.raw` 0 to 16383, as the two bytes carry it. `bend.channel` is 1 to 16 and `bend.from` the device. Raised at most once every 10 ms per channel, with the latest value.","group":""},"qa04_lua_pressureIn":{"id":"qa04_lua_pressureIn","name":"lua: onPressureIn","language":"lua","source":"function onPressureIn(pressure)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onPressureIn","enabled":true,"description":"Channel pressure arrived. `pressure.value` is 0 to 127, `pressure.amount` 0 to 1, `pressure.channel` 1 to 16 and `pressure.from` the device. Raised at most once every 10 ms per channel.","group":""},"qa04_lua_polyPressureIn":{"id":"qa04_lua_polyPressureIn","name":"lua: onPolyPressureIn","language":"lua","source":"function onPolyPressureIn(pressure)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onPolyPressureIn","enabled":true,"description":"Pressure on one note arrived. `pressure.note` is the note, `pressure.value` 0 to 127, `pressure.amount` 0 to 1, `pressure.channel` 1 to 16 and `pressure.from` the device. Raised at most once every 10 ms per note.","group":""},"qa04_lua_programIn":{"id":"qa04_lua_programIn","name":"lua: onProgramIn","language":"lua","source":"function onProgramIn(program)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onProgramIn","enabled":true,"description":"A program change arrived. `program.program` is 0 to 127, as the message carries it, and `program.number` 1 to 128, as most synths show it. `program.bankMsb` and `program.bankLsb` are the bank select that came just before it on this channel, when one did. `program.channel` is 1 to 16 and `program.from` the device.","group":""},"qa04_lua_nrpnIn":{"id":"qa04_lua_nrpnIn","name":"lua: onNrpnIn","language":"lua","source":"function onNrpnIn(nrpn)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onNrpnIn","enabled":true,"description":"An NRPN arrived, put together from its controllers (99, 98, then 6 and 38). `nrpn.msb` and `nrpn.lsb` are the parameter number's halves, as sendNRPN takes them, and `nrpn.parameter` the two as one number. `nrpn.value` is 0 to 16383 when the fine half came (`nrpn.fine` true), else 0 to 127. For an increment or decrement, `nrpn.step` is 1 or -1 instead. The controllers still raise ccIn too.","group":""},"qa04_lua_rpnIn":{"id":"qa04_lua_rpnIn","name":"lua: onRpnIn","language":"lua","source":"function onRpnIn(rpn)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onRpnIn","enabled":true,"description":"An RPN arrived, put together from controllers 101 and 100, then 6 and 38. The fields are those of nrpnIn, and `rpn.name` is \"bendRange\", \"fineTuning\", \"coarseTuning\" or \"mpeConfiguration\" for the numbers that have one.","group":""},"qa04_lua_transportIn":{"id":"qa04_lua_transportIn","name":"lua: onTransportIn","language":"lua","source":"function onTransportIn(transport)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onTransportIn","enabled":true,"description":"A device sent start, stop, continue or a song position. `transport.action` is \"start\", \"stop\", \"continue\" or \"position\"; for \"position\", `transport.beat` is where it points, in beats from the start. `transport.from` is the device. Clock ticks are not raised one by one.","group":""},"qa04_lua_expressionIn":{"id":"qa04_lua_expressionIn","name":"lua: onExpressionIn","language":"lua","source":"function onExpressionIn(expression)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onExpressionIn","enabled":true,"description":"A note read with ce.mpe.listen() moved. `expression.id` is the note's id, as noteIn gave it, `expression.note` the note and `expression.channel` its member channel. `expression.bend` is in semitones, `expression.pressure` and `expression.timbre` 0 to 1, and `expression.changed` says which moved: \"bend\", \"pressure\" or \"timbre\". Raised at most once every 10 ms per note.","group":""},"qa04_lua_sysexIn":{"id":"qa04_lua_sysexIn","name":"lua: onSysexIn","language":"lua","source":"function onSysexIn(bytes)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onSysexIn","enabled":true,"description":"A SysEx message arrived. `bytes` holds it as a list of numbers.","group":""},"qa04_lua_deviceConnected":{"id":"qa04_lua_deviceConnected","name":"lua: onDeviceConnected","language":"lua","source":"function onDeviceConnected(device)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onDeviceConnected","enabled":true,"description":"A synth was connected and is ready. `device.role` names it and `device.profileId` its profile.","group":""},"qa04_lua_deviceDisconnected":{"id":"qa04_lua_deviceDisconnected","name":"lua: onDeviceDisconnected","language":"lua","source":"function onDeviceDisconnected(device)\n  \nend\n","scope":"panel","target":"*","event":"onDeviceDisconnected","enabled":true,"description":"A synth is no longer connected and ready. `device.role` names it, and `device.message` may say why.","group":""},"qa04_lua_step":{"id":"qa04_lua_step","name":"lua: onStep","language":"lua","source":"function onStep(step)\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onStep","enabled":true,"description":"A sequencer moved to its next step: an Arpeggiator, Turing Machine, Phrase Sequencer or Looper. `step.target` is its name, `step.index` the step, counted from 1, `step.of` how many there are, and `step.notes` the notes it plays.","group":""},"qa04_lua_cycle":{"id":"qa04_lua_cycle","name":"lua: onCycle","language":"lua","source":"function onCycle(cycle)\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onCycle","enabled":true,"description":"A sequence or loop came round to its start: an Arpeggiator, Turing Machine, Looper or Orbit. `cycle.target` is its name and `cycle.count` how many times it has come round since the panel opened.","group":""},"qa04_lua_hit":{"id":"qa04_lua_hit","name":"lua: onHit","language":"lua","source":"function onHit(hit)\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onHit","enabled":true,"description":"A pad, key or strip was struck: a Chord Pad, Drum Pads or Note Ribbon. `hit.target` is its name, `hit.id` which pad or key, `hit.note` the note and `hit.velocity` how hard.","group":""},"qa04_lua_release":{"id":"qa04_lua_release","name":"lua: onRelease","language":"lua","source":"function onRelease(release)\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onRelease","enabled":true,"description":"A pad, key or strip was let go. `release.target` is its name, `release.id` which pad or key, and `release.note` the note.","group":""},"qa04_lua_scene":{"id":"qa04_lua_scene","name":"lua: onScene","language":"lua","source":"function onScene(scene)\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onScene","enabled":true,"description":"The Setlist moved to a scene, however it was chosen. `scene.target` is its name, `scene.index` the scene, counted from 1, and `scene.name` its name.","group":""},"qa04_lua_stage":{"id":"qa04_lua_stage","name":"lua: onStage","language":"lua","source":"function onStage(stage)\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onStage","enabled":true,"description":"A Recorder or an Envelope moved to a new stage. `stage.target` is its name, `stage.stage` the new stage and `stage.previous` the old one: the Recorder's \"idle\", \"armed\", \"recording\" and \"overdub\", the Envelope's \"sustain\", \"release\" and \"end\". Not onStateChanged, which is hover and press.","group":""},"qa04_lua_settled":{"id":"qa04_lua_settled","name":"lua: onSettled","language":"lua","source":"function onSettled(settled)\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onSettled","enabled":true,"description":"A Ribbon, Crossfader or Vector Joystick finished going back to its rest. `settled.target` is its name and `settled.value` where it came to rest.","group":""},"qa04_lua_bounce":{"id":"qa04_lua_bounce","name":"lua: onBounce","language":"lua","source":"function onBounce(bounce)\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onBounce","enabled":true,"description":"The Kinetic ball hit a wall. `bounce.target` is its name, `bounce.x` and `bounce.y` where it hit, and `bounce.vx` and `bounce.vy` its speed across and down.","group":""},"qa04_lua_recall":{"id":"qa04_lua_recall","name":"lua: onRecall","language":"lua","source":"function onRecall(recall)\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onRecall","enabled":true,"description":"The Constellation, in snap mode, moved to another preset. `recall.target` is its name, `recall.id` the preset and `recall.label` its label.","group":""},"qa04_lua_zone":{"id":"qa04_lua_zone","name":"lua: onZone","language":"lua","source":"function onZone(zone)\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onZone","enabled":true,"description":"A Meter's reading crossed into another zone, such as from green into red. `zone.target` is its name, `zone.zone` the new zone, `zone.previous` the old one and `zone.value` the reading.","group":""},"qa04_lua_voiced":{"id":"qa04_lua_voiced","name":"lua: onVoiced","language":"lua","source":"function onVoiced(voiced)\n  \nend\n","scope":"component","target":"self","event":"onVoiced","enabled":true,"description":"A Zone Splitter or Harmoniser turned a played note into other notes. `voiced.target` is its name, `voiced.note` and `voiced.velocity` the note played, and `voiced.out` the notes it made.","group":""}}}
